DAY 23 – METHODS AND CONSTRUCTORS

1. INSTANCE METHOD

An Instance Method works with object data.

It uses self as the first parameter.

self refers to the current object.


2. CLASS METHOD

A Class Method works with class-level data.

It uses cls as the first parameter.

cls refers to the class itself.


3. STATIC METHOD

A Static Method is independent of object and class data.

It is mainly used for utility tasks.


4. CONSTRUCTOR

A constructor is used to initialize objects
when they are created.

In Python, __init__() is used as a constructor.


5. NON-PARAMETERIZED CONSTRUCTOR

A Non-Parameterized Constructor is a constructor
without parameters apart from self.

It is used when the object does not need any
external values during initialization.


6. PARAMETERIZED CONSTRUCTOR

A Parameterized Constructor is a constructor that
accepts parameters to initialize object data.

It allows different objects to be initialized
with different values.


7. TYPES OF METHODS

Python OOP mainly has three types of methods:

• Instance Method
• Class Method
• Static Method


8. INSTANCE METHOD vs CLASS METHOD vs STATIC METHOD

Instance Method
→ Works with object data
→ Uses self

Class Method
→ Works with class-level data
→ Uses cls

Static Method
→ Independent of object and class data
→ Mainly used for utility tasks


9. CONSTRUCTOR TYPES

• Non-Parameterized Constructor
• Parameterized Constructor


KEY TAKEAWAY

Instance Method → Object data → self

Class Method → Class-level data → cls

Static Method → Independent of object and class

Constructor → Initializes objects

